The vertical electrical sounding (VES) reveals a four-layer subsurface model with resistivity increasing monotonically with depth. The resistivity values for the layers are 640 $\Omega$m, 934 $\Omega$m, 2594 $\Omega$m, and 4386 $\Omega$m, respectively. Following the curve-type notation, the first three-layer group (1-2-3) shows an increasing trend (A), and the second group (2-3-4) also shows an increasing trend (A). This results in an AA curve type. The classification of AA-type currently on file is accurate and consistent with the interpreted layer resistivity values.

