Station Okehi, Etche LGA, consists of a four-layer subsurface sequence. The resistivity profile begins at 697.56 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$ (Layer 1), rises sharply to 10,642 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$ (Layer 2), decreases to 5,533 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$ (Layer 3), and shows a slight increase to 5,776.1 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$ (Layer 4). 

Applying the curve-type notation: the transition between layers 1, 2, and 3 follows an increase-then-decrease pattern (K), while the transition between layers 2, 3, and 4 follows a decrease-then-increase pattern (H). This defines the curve as KH-type, which is consistent with the classification currently held on file.

