Station: BMGS-bori-field, Bori Metropolis.

The vertical electrical sounding (VES) interpretation reveals a six-layer subsurface sequence. The resistivity profile begins at 1005 $\Omega$m, increases to 3588 $\Omega$m in the second layer, and then decreases through the third layer to a minimum of 333 $\Omega$m in the fourth layer. Following this low-resistivity zone, the resistivity increases again through layers five and six. The calculated curve type is KQHA, which is in full agreement with the KQHA-type classification currently on file.

{"curve_type_stated": "KQHA", "label_issue_flagged": false}

