Site Report: Kenpoly-sec-school-field, Bori Metropolis.

The vertical electrical sounding (VES) interpretation for this station identifies a five-layer subsurface sequence. The resistivity profile begins at 1874 ohm-m, increases to 2428 ohm-m in the second layer, decreases to 1071 ohm-m in the third, rises significantly to 3706 ohm-m in the fourth layer, and drops to 178 ohm-m in the fifth layer. Based on these resistivity transitions, the calculated curve type is KHK (K for layers 1-2-3, H for layers 2-3-4, and K for layers 3-4-5). This calculation is consistent with the survey interpretation currently on file.

