Station Kogam-street, Bori Metropolis. The interpreted subsurface sequence consists of five layers. The resistivity starts at 127 ohm-m (0.82m), decreases to 50.4 ohm-m in the second layer (6.45m depth), and then increases progressively through the third layer (126 ohm-m), fourth layer (149 ohm-m), and fifth layer (197 ohm-m). 

Applying the curve-type notation, the first three layers (127, 50.4, 126) follow an H pattern (r1 > r2 < r3). The subsequent groups—layers 2-3-4 (50.4, 126, 149) and layers 3-4-5 (126, 149, 197)—both follow an A pattern (r1 < r2 < r3). Therefore, the resulting curve type is HAA, which is consistent with the survey interpretation currently on file.

