The interpreted geophysical profile consists of four layers. The sequence begins with a 1.23m top layer at 150 ohm-m, followed by a 6.21m layer of lower resistivity at 97.1 ohm-m. This is succeeded by a 37.5m thick layer with 284 ohm-m, leading into a high-resistivity basal layer of 700 ohm-m. Evaluating the resistivity transitions (150 > 97.1 < 284 and 97.1 < 284 < 700) yields an HA curve type. This is consistent with the station's current classification on file.

