Station: Kor-road, Bori Metropolis. The vertical electrical sounding (VES) interpretation reveals a four-layer subsurface model. The resistivity sequence begins at 1916 ohm-m (Layer 1, 1.24m), decreases to 1252 ohm-m (Layer 2, 3.03m), increases to 1658 ohm-m (Layer 3, 111m), and finally decreases to 581 ohm-m (Layer 4). 

Applying the curve-type notation rules: the first group of three layers (1916 > 1252 < 1658) follows an H-pattern, and the second group (1252 < 1658 > 581) follows a K-pattern. This results in an HK-type curve. The existing file classification of HK-type is accurate and matches the interpreted resistivity values.

{"curve_type_stated": "HK", "label_issue_flagged": false}

