parts.text:
Station Odufor, located in Etche LGA, consists of a four-layer subsurface sequence. The layer resistivities are 20.32 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$, 851.16 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$, 2511.9 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$, and 1345 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$. 

Applying the curve-type notation: the first three layers (1-2-3) show a continuous increase in resistivity (20.32 < 851.16 < 2511.9), which corresponds to an "A" type. The subsequent group (2-3-4) shows a resistivity peak (851.16 < 2511.9 > 1345), which corresponds to a "K" type. Consequently, the calculated curve type is AK. This is in full agreement with the AK-type classification recorded in the current survey interpretation on file.

{"curve_type_stated": "AK", "label_issue_flagged": false}

